name 'building-data-driven-systems-postassessment-q6_2025'

question 'You are testing a helper function `addItem(newItem)`. The AI generates a test case where `newItem` is an empty string "". Why is this a valuable test?'

wrong 'It tests if the AI can handle strings.'
right 'It is an edge case that ensures the function doesn\'t add "blank" items to the user\'s list.'
wrong 'Empty strings are the most common type of data in professional apps.'
wrong 'It proves that the `.map()` function is working correctly.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 3

 Validation within helper functions should prevent "bad" data (like empty strings) from entering the dataset. Testing this edge case ensures the function is robust.
MARKDOWN
